      "notes": "This is a dark fantasy tragedy about a man condemned for a crime he did not commit.\r\nThe story deals with heavy subject matter throughout.\r\n\r\nVIOLENCE\r\nThe game depicts execution by hanging, mob violence, stabbing, burning, poisoning, and\r\nthe killing of a child. One route includes combat with severe bodily injury. All of this\r\nis conveyed through written prose and still character art. There is no animated gore.\r\n\r\nSEXUAL CONTENT\r\nThere is no sexual imagery in this game. No nudity is depicted and no sexual act is ever\r\nshown. Sexual content exists only as references in the text, and every instance is\r\npresented as an act of harm:\r\n- A past sexual assault (non-consensual sex) forms part of the story's background and is\r\n  referred to in dialogue.\r\n- A character is verbally degraded with sexual insults.\r\n- A character works as a prostitute; coercion involving her is discussed.\r\n- One route depicts sustained emotional abuse within a marriage.\r\nNone of this is presented approvingly or for titillation. The narrative consistently\r\nframes these acts as cruelty, and the suffering they cause is the subject of the story.\r\n\r\nOTHER SENSITIVE CONTENT\r\n- Self-harm and a past suicide attempt are described by a character recalling his history.\r\n- Alcohol is consumed on screen, mostly by characters abusing their authority.\r\n- Wrongful conviction, false testimony, persecution by a mob, imprisonment, and child\r\n  abuse are central themes.\r\n\r\nThe game does not glorify any of the above. Every act of violence and abuse is shown to\r\nhave consequences, and the story treats them as tragedy rather than spectacle."
    }
